# Normalize line endings to LF for everything text-based, regardless
# of a given contributor's or CI runner's local git config (core.autocrlf
# etc.) — without this, a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true can commit
# or check out CRLF line endings for files that were authored as LF,
# which is invisible in most diffs/editors but makes tools with strict
# formatting expectations (prettier's default endOfLine: "lf") fail in
# CI even though the file content otherwise matches byte-for-byte.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files some tools might otherwise try to "normalize" —
# explicit is safer than relying on file-extension heuristics alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
